Subject: [PATCH] misc: fastrpc: Allocate message buffer from remote heap for sensors PD

Backport the one-line change proposed by Robin Snyders and submitted by
Piyush Raj Chouhan, reviewed by Dmitry Baryshkov:

https://lore.kernel.org/linux-arm-msm/20261003150559.6926-2-pc1598@mainlining.org/
https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2026/10/03/762
https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2026/10/05/99

The sensors PD needs the message buffer allocated through the remote-heap
path even when the session has a context-bank ID. Otherwise attaching can
fault at an unmapped IOVA such as 0x1fffff000 and crash sensor_process.

Only the hunk offset has been adapted to v7.2.6. Tested upstream on other
SM8150 devices; hardware validation on nabu is still required.

diff --git a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -1052,7 +1052,7 @@
 
 	ctx->msg_sz = pkt_size;
 
-	if (ctx->fl->sctx->sid)
+	if (ctx->fl->sctx->sid && ctx->fl->pd != SENSORS_PD)
 		err = fastrpc_buf_alloc(ctx->fl, dev, pkt_size, &ctx->buf);
 	else
 		err = fastrpc_remote_heap_alloc(ctx->fl, dev, pkt_size, &ctx->buf);
